      <uighur>qaγorai</uighur>
      <cyrillic>хуурай</cyrillic>
      <transcript>XAΓURAI</transcript>
      <definition>1 [= xuγurai] adj. and n. Dry, dried up; dry land; dryness, drought</definition>
      <page>910</page>
      <examples>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠬᠠᠭᠣᠷᠠᠢ ᠪᠣᠯᠭᠠᠬᠤ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- bolγaxu</transcript>
          <definition> To make dry, drain (as marshland).</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠬᠠᠭᠣᠷᠠᠢ ᠪᠤᠳᠠᠭ᠎ᠠ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- budaγ-a</transcript>
          <definition> Dry precooked millet (Ch. ch'ao-mi</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠬᠠᠭᠣᠷᠠᠢ ᠡᠪᠡᠰᠦ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- ebesy</transcript>
          <definition> Hay, dry grass.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠬᠠᠭᠣᠷᠠᠢ ᠡᠴᠢᠺᠡ ~ ᠬᠠᠭᠣᠷᠠᠢ ᠡᠺᠡ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- ecige / eke </transcript>
          <definition> 'Dry' father or mother: a person chosen by a child's parents to bring him good fortune (Ch. kan-tieh, kan-niang); the father or mother of a 'sworn brother'</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠬᠠᠭᠣᠷᠠᠢ ᠭᠠᠵᠠᠷ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- γazar</transcript>
          <definition> Dry land; continent, mainland.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠬᠠᠭᠣᠷᠠᠢ ᠢᠳᠡᠰᠢ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- idesi</transcript>
          <definition> Dry food.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠬᠠᠭᠣᠷᠠᠢ ᠺᠦᠪᠡᠭᠦᠨ ~ ᠬᠠᠭᠣᠷᠠᠢ ᠺᠡᠦᠺᠡᠨ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- kybegyn / keyken</transcript>
          <definition> Chosen child. Cf. xaγurai ecige.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠬᠠᠭᠣᠷᠠᠢ ᠮᠣᠳᠤ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- modu</transcript>
          <definition> Dry tree, dry wood.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠬᠠᠭᠣᠷᠠᠢ ᠬᠣᠭᠤᠯᠠᠢ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- xoγulai</transcript>
          <definition> Windpipe.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠬᠠᠭᠣᠷᠠᠢ ᠵᠠᠮ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- zam</transcript>
          <definition> Overland route.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠬᠠᠭᠣᠷᠠᠢ ᠵᠠᠮ ᠤᠨ ᠴᠡᠷᠢᠭ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- zamun cerig</transcript>
          <definition> Land troops, ground forces</definition>
        </example>
